    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI updated the membership-level rule in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/MembershipLevels.java` so that **level 4 requires tenure of more than 365 days**.\n\n**What changed:**\n- The email and `namesakeCount == 0` factors still cap out at level 3 (`Math.min(level, 3)`).\n- A new gate promotes a level-3 owner to level 4 **only** when tenure exceeds 365 days.\n- Tenure is derived as the number of days from the owner's `registrationDate` to today (`ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(...)`), with a null-safe fallback of zero.\n\n**Why a new owner never exceeds level 3:** `ResolveRegistrationDate`/`BuildOwner` stamp a new owner's `registrationDate` as today (or a non-future supplied date), so its tenure is 0 \u2014 well under 366 \u2014 and the level-4 promotion never fires. A new owner with an email, `namesakeCount` of 0, and a 3-member household therefore lands at level 3, exactly as the spec and the `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` acceptance test require.\n\nThe doc comment on the class was updated to describe the tenure requirement, replacing the old \"Level 4 is reserved for tenure and is not assigned here\" note.",
